  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Two libraries, both files",
      "items": [
        "The Public Library is markdown in site/library/, versioned in Git and shipped with each deploy. Nothing in the app writes to it: POST, PUT and DELETE on /api/prompts all go to My Library.",
        "My Library is a local folder, site/my-library/ unless MY_LIBRARY_DIR moves it, with one markdown file per prompt and its title, section, category and tags in frontmatter. There are no accounts: the server listens on 127.0.0.1, and on the Vercel demo READ_ONLY refuses every write.",
        "Add to My Library reads the public file, strips its frontmatter, refuses a duplicate title in the same section and category, and writes a copy as a new file whose name is its id."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Why the listing carries no bodies",
      "items": [
        "The lightweight public listing comes from prompt-index.json with every content field emptied, and is cached in the function for 5 minutes.",
        "Cards ask POST /api/prompts/previews for the blurbs they render (up to 200 ids per request), served from the index's 200-character previews with a file fallback.",
        "The real body comes from GET /api/prompts/:id, fetched when a prompt is opened, copied, downloaded or edited."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Skill packs",
      "items": [
        "Pack manifests are JSON under library/3_Skills/packs, each listing its skills' SKILL.md paths. api/skill-packs.ts is its own Vercel function, bundled with library/3_Skills/**.",
        "Add to library copies every skill in the pack into My Library, tagged skill-pack:<id>, and skips ones already there; that tag is how the My Library pack list knows a pack is installed. Download zips each skill's whole directory.",
        "A single skill's directory also downloads as a ZIP from GET /api/skills/download/:path, which refuses any path outside 3_Skills/."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Where the content comes from",
      "items": [
        "Vendored skills and agents carry an upstream: block. The weekly Upstream drift workflow reports which are behind in one GitHub issue and never edits the library; resync-upstream.mjs is run by hand to pull a body back level.",
        "After any library change, npm run build:index regenerates the index. CI rebuilds it and fails when the committed file differs, and vercel-build rebuilds it on every deploy."
      ]
    }
  ]
